.TITLE "head"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the first part of a file. It outputs the __beginning lines__ of text files, which is useful for previewing file content.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**head file**
Displays the first ten lines of a file.
> __file__ the target path

**head -n 20 file**
Displays a specific number of lines from the start of a file.
> __-n__ line count flag | __20__ number of lines

**head -c 100 file**
Displays the first specified number of bytes from a file.
> __-c__ byte count flag | __100__ number of bytes

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __head__ command is perfect for quickly inspecting the headers of data files without loading the entire content into memory. Use it in combination with __tail__ to extract specific ranges of lines from a file.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:tail** **mac:cat**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/head.html__
